hermes v0.23.0: a background process a delegate_task subagent starts
never wakes the parent's TUI/Desktop/dashboard session.

Symptom: when a subagent's terminal(background=true) command ends, the
parent session gets a new turn "[IMPORTANT: Background process proc_...
completed normally ... Started by subagent sa-... of delegation ...]",
although the child was told (subagent_note) that its notice will NOT
reach the parent.

Cause: the child's process carries the parent's session_key, so the
parent's notification poller (tui_gateway/session_notifications.py
_notif_handle_event) proves ownership and dispatches it. Every other
drain (ProcessRegistry.drain_notifications, the gateway watchers, the
post-turn safety net in prompt_turn.py) filters child-owned processes
with should_surface_notification (delegation.
surface_child_process_notifications, default false); this poller did not.

Fix: apply the same policy there; a suppressed notice is dropped, not
requeued (children never drain). Handed-off processes are re-owned by
the parent and still notify it; the parent's own processes are
unchanged; the opt-in flag still surfaces child processes.

